# {{title}} — Apify Actor

{{tagline}}

Grocery prices from Brazilian supermarket websites, collected weekly.

This Actor is a thin pass-through. It calls the {{name}} REST API at {{api_base_url}} and stores
the API answer in the run's dataset. Nothing is scraped inside the Actor, so runs are short and
cheap. You do not need an API key: the Actor holds its own.

Coverage: {{facts.stores}} store units in {{facts.states}} states of Brazil, as of {{facts.as_of}}.
Prices are advertised online prices in BRL and are weekly observations, not a live feed.

## Input

- `tool` (required): one of the 11 API tools.
- `params` (object): arguments for the chosen tool, named as in the API. For a `POST` tool such as
  `compare_basket`, the request body goes here.

```json
{
  "tool": "search_products",
  "params": {"query": "milk", "city": "Sao Paulo", "state": "SP"}
}
```

## Example — lookup event

Input:

```json
{
  "tool": "search_products",
  "params": {"query": "white rice 5kg", "city": "Sao Paulo", "state": "SP"}
}
```

The Actor calls `GET /api/v1/products/search?query=white+rice+5kg&city=Sao+Paulo&state=SP` and
stores the answer in the dataset, shortened here:

```json
{
  "as_of": "2026-11-19T02:30:00Z",
  "country": "BR",
  "currency": "BRL",
  "attribution": "Retail prices observed on retailer websites by {{name}} ({{site_url}}).",
  "truncated": false,
  "products": [
    {
      "product_id": 1024,
      "ean": "7891000100103",
      "ean_verified": true,
      "name": "White rice type 1 5kg",
      "brand": "Example Brand",
      "size": "5kg",
      "category": "Grains",
      "url": "{{site_url}}/produto/white-rice-5kg",
      "min_price": 24.9,
      "max_price": 31.5,
      "store_count": 4,
      "last_seen": "2026-11-18T23:30:00-03:00"
    }
  ],
  "next_cursor": null
}
```

Billed: one `lookup` event, US$ 0.003.

## Example — analytics event

Input:

```json
{
  "tool": "compare_basket",
  "params": {
    "city": "Sao Paulo",
    "items": [{"query": "white rice 5kg"}, {"ean": "7891000100103"}]
  }
}
```

The Actor calls `POST /api/v1/baskets/compare` with the body above and stores the answer,
shortened here:

```json
{
  "as_of": "2026-11-19T02:30:00Z",
  "country": "BR",
  "currency": "BRL",
  "attribution": "Retail prices observed on retailer websites by {{name}} ({{site_url}}).",
  "truncated": false,
  "stores": [
    {
      "store": {"store_id": 17, "chain": "Example Chain", "unit": "Sao Paulo"},
      "total": 182.4,
      "items_found": 2,
      "items_missing": []
    }
  ],
  "matched_products": [],
  "best_store": {
    "store": {"store_id": 17, "chain": "Example Chain", "unit": "Sao Paulo"},
    "total": 182.4,
    "complete": true
  },
  "best_split": null
}
```

Billed: one `analytics` event, US$ 0.015.

## Pricing

- `lookup` — US$ 0.003 per successful call: `search_products`, `get_product`, `get_prices`,
  `list_baskets`, `list_locations`, `list_stores`, `list_categories`.
- `analytics` — US$ 0.015 per successful call: `compare_basket`, `get_price_history`,
  `get_basket`, `get_price_index`.

One run makes one API call and is billed at most one event.

## Limits and behaviour

- A call is charged only after a 2xx answer from the API. Errors such as 404, 429 or 5xx are
  written to the dataset as the API sent them and are not charged.
- The API has a 15-second timeout per call; a slow call fails and is not charged.
- The API applies its own rate limits. A limited call (429) is not charged.
- The history starts in March 2026, so year-over-year comparisons are not possible yet.
- Products without a verified barcode are matched by name and flagged (`ean_verified: false`).
  No photos or retailer descriptions are returned.
- Data is provided as is. These are advertised online prices, not the price on the physical
  shelf. Attribute the source when republishing it: {{name}} ({{site_url}}).
